text:
A Counter displays a number along with buttons to change it. The min and max props limit the range of allowed values: import { Counter } from "sample-lib";

function CounterBasicExample() {
 return (
 <Counter
 initialValue={0}
 max={10}
 min={0}
 />
 );
} Count: - 0 + The value can also be changed programmatically using the imperative handle.

headings.text:
Example import { useRef } from "react";
import { Counter, type CounterImperativeHandle } from "sample-lib";

function CounterImperativeHandleExample() {
 const counterRef = useRef<CounterImperativeHandle>(null);

 return (
 <>
 <Counter counterRef={counterRef} initialValue={5} />
 <Button onClick={() => counterRef.current?.reset()}>Reset</Button>
 </>
 );
} Count: - 5 + Reset

Theming Badges accept a className for additional styles: .my-badge {
 border: 1px solid currentColor;
 letter-spacing: 0.05em;
 text-transform: uppercase;
}

text:
Use the intent prop to change the color of a badge: import { Badge } from "sample-lib";

function BadgeIntentsExample() {
 return (
 <>
 <Badge>Neutral</Badge>
 <Badge intent="success">Success</Badge>
 <Badge intent="warning">Warning</Badge>
 <Badge intent="danger">Danger</Badge>
 </>
 );
} Neutral Success Warning Danger

headings.text:
Can I customize how badges look? Yes. Pass a className and style it with CSS: .my-badge {
 border: 1px solid currentColor;
 letter-spacing: 0.05em;
 text-transform: uppercase;
}
